## Open questions

Bounded completion: both gene-regulatory and protein-environment branches have evidence; their predominant contribution is not identified by unmatched assays. Reverse PMP22 loss supports a lipid/efflux phenotype but is not a closed transcriptional feedback loop. Retinoid, broad metabolic signaling and human transfer remain deferred beyond this first task, not disproven.

The saved bidirectionality design crosses independent sterol/receptor intervention with acute PMP22 dose/ABCA1 perturbation and near-endogenous addback, and keeps endocrine PR/metabolite routes separate. It requires early calibrated endogenous P1/P2 nascent output, mature RNA/decay, synthesis/turnover, absolute surface/myelin delivery, efflux and function, with state/viability, sex, donor and age controls. Preventive and adult-onset rescue cohorts are distinct. No experiment was executed. No invented sample size or equivalence margin is supplied; independent pilot variance is required.

Additional full-text endocrine audit completed on PMC3315401: male Sprague-Dawley 180-210g rats, trigeminal LPA injury, 16mg/kg/day progesterone from operation for five days, immunohistochemistry and immunoblot n=5/group. Figure7's 19kDa PMP22 band and GAPDH loading control measure immunoreactive protein, not RNA or synthesis. This reinforces endpoint separation; chronic age and cross-assay pairing remain unresolved. Nature PMID14608378 full-text request returned HTTP200 Client Challenge, not the article; Wiley PMID16787508 returned HTTP403. Both remain abstract-limited. No challenge bypass or downloaded code execution occurred.

